Fillets and chamfers: a stripe's OnSame end whose prolonged edge runs along
a seam of the opposite face (mitcad#263).

The case: a lug inside a bore, its top's concave edge with the bore's
wall chamfered or rounded as wide as the top (0140), the lug ending at the
bore's seam. ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner prolongs the edge between the
lug's end and the wall (left from the seam by the join of the lug, used
once by the wall but keeping both p-curves) up to the blend's contact:

- the prolongation's p-curve on the wall was taken from the edge's p-curve
  for its orientation, not for the wall's use of it: the prolongation lay
  on the seam's other side, where the blend covers the wall. It is now
  taken as the wall uses the edge;
- the seam above the corner's vertex was not cut: the wall kept the seam
  along the prolongation on both sides, and its wire intersected itself.
  Where the prolongation runs along a seam of the opposite face from the
  corner's vertex, the seam is now cut at the prolongation's end and its
  part along it kept on neither side (ChFi3d_CutSeamAlongCurve).

Before, the blend of the case gave a self-intersecting wire.

